content:
Connect to DrorPay using Socket.IO:
```js
const io = require('socket.io-client');
const socket = io('ws://your-drorpay-server.com');
```

Recommended flow — join the payment room BEFORE creating the payment intent:
```js
socket.emit('join-payment-room', {
  platform_order_id: 'your-order-123',
  platform_id: 'your-platform-uuid'
});

socket.on('payment-room-joined', (data) => {
  console.log('Room joined for:', data.platform_order_id);
  // Now call create-intent — no race condition possible
  createPaymentIntent();
});
```

Why join first: the current implementation auto-completes payments immediately after creation. If you join after the API call, the payment may complete before your socket listener is active.

Two ways to join a payment room:

Option 1 (recommended): Use platform_order_id BEFORE creating the intent
```js
socket.emit('join-payment-room', {
  platform_order_id: 'your-order-123',
  platform_id: 'your-platform-uuid'
});
```
This is recommended because it eliminates the race condition — the socket room is ready before the payment is created.

Option 2: Use platform_transaction_id AFTER creating the intent
```js
socket.emit('join-payment-room', {
  platform_transaction_id: 'uuid-from-create-intent-response',
  platform_id: 'your-platform-uuid'
});
```
Risk: the payment may auto-complete before you join, causing you to miss the events.
